meta {
  name: Delete my account
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/privacy/erasure
  body: json
}

body:json {
  {
    "password": "a-long-enough-password",
    "confirm": true,
    "reason": "Moving abroad."
  }
}

docs {
  Re-checks the password: it is the one irreversible action on the platform.

  Schedules erasure for the end of a grace period (14 days by default) and
  emails and texts the account holder — which is the point, because the case
  this is really designed for is a stolen session asking for a deletion.

  Financial and legal records survive without personal details attached. See
  `docs/DATA_RETENTION.md` for exactly what is kept and why.
}
